 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "15-17 are the Prophet's ﷺ words: no motif there. Their demand (15:11-16) is framed («وطلبوا وجوه التعنت… جراءة منهم وظلما»). Al-Muyassar's first-person «لننظر… فنجازيكم» is not used. Mountains for the earth they inherit (no name of Allah in 14), an hourglass for «لننظر كيف تعملون», a book for «تتلى عليهم آياتنا». STAGING v4: c1 (14) is staged in a town by day: a small mixed group of people (the address is to people in general, Al-Muyassar) walks in and settles (successors in the land after the destroyed generations, who are not drawn: no ruins); an hourglass plate on 14:8 for the time of their test. c2 (15-16) stays ambient: the demand to change the Quran is addressed to the Prophet (never shown) and 15:17-16:18 are his commanded words, so nobody is drawn and the background stays quiet over them; a book plate on 15:2 for the verses recited. c3 (17) is kept ambient (the greatest wrong and the criminals' failure, a general statement)."
 },
